{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1187489-am-i-missing-something","id":1187489,"title":"Am I missing something?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-19T01:10:29-08:00","id":1187489,"title":"Am I missing something?","content":"Argos 2 Wayfarer's Resolve says &quot;Many wraiths find travel into the deeper Underworld constrained by the spiritual weight of their Fetters. This art frees its user to move between the Shadowlands and Tempest-bounded destinations without suffering this constraint. System: The wraith ignores the difficulty penalties that normally apply outside the Shadowlands while she has unresolved Fetters.&quot; I can't seem to find anything about these constraints and penalties. There is a mention of being tied to the Shadowlands for an number of days equal to ones highest Fetter rating, but that seems rather situational and lackluster for an Initiate art.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T04:30:36-08:00","id":1187514,"title":"","content":"Yeah...sounds like this one should be in the errata thread","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T05:21:51-08:00","id":1187518,"title":"","content":"There's supposed to be a difficulty increase on all actions in the Tempest if you have unresolved fetters. Conversely, older wraiths without fetters get the difficulty increase if they travel to the Shadowlands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T07:49:14-08:00","id":1187549,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">There were mechanics for that sort of thing in WtO Second (not sure about First). My guess: it's a power designed to circumvent this, but the actual mechanics in Wr20 may have ended up in a nihil. I'll check WtO 2nd for a reference.<br /> <br /> Edit: <i>Wraith: the Oblivion, Second Edition</i>, page 231, &quot;Underworld Travel.&quot;<br /> <br /> I remember hating this rule and ignoring it, but now that Argos as a power that specifically mitigates it, I think I might start using it. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":302,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","user":"Nazfool","date":". 02-19-2018, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T08:01:11-08:00","id":1187554,"title":"","content":"On the plus side, they made it clear whether it was resolving one fetter or resolving all of them that allowed Wraiths to travel anywhere. Although they don't clarify whether Wraiths with all Fetters resolved still face difficulty penalties in the Shadowlands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T13:29:30-08:00","id":1187631,"title":"","content":"We really need to get them to make sure all basic facts concerning freedom of Underworld travel are spelled out, because this is the kind of thing that many of us hoped would be cleared up in Wr20","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2